## Cost estimate — 10 arms (9 + pilot) x 3 calls, weighted tokens (harness/tokens.py weights: 1 / 1.25 / 0.1 / 5)
Anchors, read from work/20/20.11/03e_score_output.json and 20.12/03e_score_output.json (launcher JSON, weighted):
  * 20.11 q94 q95 q96 = protocol installed, SILENT prompt (the prompt_t1 is byte-identical to 20.11's prompt.txt; 20.11's P side was sent this one, 20.12/01_think.md): 151,036 / 132,177 / 123,621 (15/20/27 turns) → mean 135,611.
  * 20.12 q100 q101 q102 = protocol named in the prompt: 170,262 / 164,420 / 165,315 → mean 166,666 (not the regime here).
  * 20.11 q97 q98 q99 = no protocol, silent prompt: 41,942 / 35,241 / 45,800 → mean 41,000 (K has the protocol, so not the anchor).
Per call (only turn 1 is measured; turn 2 and session 2 are ASSUMPTIONS, stated as such):
  * turn 1 = the 20.11 protocol/silent arm: 135.6k (range 123.6k–151.0k).
  * turn 2 (`--resume`, a context of ~60k tokens read from cache at 0.1 per API call, 3–8 calls, a small write, ~1.5k output x 5): ~20k (K, mostly a reply) to ~70k (E/R writing the block and reading rules); point 40k.
  * session 2 (fresh session: restore + build a button + test): 60k–130k; point 90k (a fresh protocol arm on a smaller task than the scoreboard; 20.11's arm cost 135.6k for the larger one).
Per arm: point 135.6 + 40 + 90 = 265.6k;  low 123.6 + 20 + 60 = 203.6k;  high 151.0 + 70 + 130 = 351.0k.
Ten arms (9 + pilot): point 10 x 265.6k = 2.66M;  low 10 x 203.6k = 2.04M;  high 10 x 351.0k = 3.51M.
  Against the ~3M cut line in 01_think.md: the point estimate (2.66M) is under it, the high end (3.51M) is over it. Not enough to cut E now; the pilot (q900, one K arm) gives the first measured t2 and s2 numbers, and check_pilot.sh prints "nine arms at that rate": if that figure plus the pilot exceeds ~3M, cut to K and R and record E as unrun. R adds a few k per reply for the footer and the write (3 replies x ~3k = ~9k per R arm, <0.1M on the round).

